lisa-design:
- Second half of T04a (stacked on #8): preview.yml, publish-image.yml, cut-prerelease.yml, internal/release NextRC and PreviewTags, cmd/release next-rc and preview-tags.
- publish-image.yml is the shared piece for T04b: a reusable workflow (inputs images JSON + space-separated tags; contents: read, packages: write), not a composite action, because a local composite action in a called workflow resolves against the caller's checkout while a local reusable workflow resolves to this repo at the same commit. It publishes whatever tags it is given; tag policy (no latest on previews, latest only for final tags) stays with the caller. T04b adds native amd64+arm64 builds and a manifest merge behind the same inputs.
- preview.yml implements the image path only; plugin/policy OCI previews via gooci are left to T04b (on-main input is already there for them). Fork PRs never publish (GITHUB_TOKEN is read-only there).
- cut-prerelease: version from the open release-please PR's manifest (exactly one release-please--branches--* PR into the default branch, else fail); rc number from the existing <prefix><version>-rcN tags (matching-refs API, digits only, so -rc.3 or -rc10x are ignored); fails if the final tag exists; gh release create --target <default branch head sha> --prerelease --latest=false with the scoped bot token so release: published fires in the caller. set -o pipefail so a failed tag listing can't produce rc1. concurrency group per repo so two dispatches can't cut the same rc.
- The token-scope guard step is duplicated in release-please.yml and cut-prerelease.yml (a token minted in one job can't be shared); internal/ciworkflows TestTokenScopeGuard pins them equal and exercises the cases.

